      "refusal_code": "unsupported_evidence_contract",
      "class": "negative",
      "note": "Recognized token, unsupported schema_version integer: the payload is otherwise shape-valid, so the refusal can only come from the version check (spec section 2.1) and pins that a correct token with a wrong version is unsupported_evidence_contract, not a silent default or an older parser. The name is historical: the case was written when the version could ride the ingress row and became inexpressible once the row dropped its token (ADR 0093 decision 10), which re-pointed it at the envelope's schema_version. Read this case as the envelope-version defect it now is, not as a snapshot-version defect."
    },
