      "direction": "consumer",
      "expect": "refuse",
      "refusal_code": "database_row_overflow",
      "class": "overflow",
      "e1_decision": "E1 rule (spec section 3): the 32 KiB serialized-snapshot bound is evaluated before the per-entry bounds, so this payload — which also breaks the 512-char field-text bound — deterministically reports the byte bound as database_row_overflow. The byte bound is a redundant transport guard, not a restatement of a field bound."
